Author: Dr. Thorsten Tepper Garcia

Created: 16 JAN 2024


	*IMPORTANT*:
		THIS PATCH (and its partent patch/tepper/dice_restart STILL HAS A NUMBER OF BUGS!
		For instance, Main step starts at 1 instead of at the actual last value; the same is true for nstep_coarse.
		Restarting a simulation (h_00_gh0_lr_ofe_wh_rs) leads to the mass of evolved, newborn stellar particles drop below their allowed minimum value.


	Last modified:

	17 JAN 2024:
	Now correctly reading particle potential, 'nmetal' metals, and initial particle mass. Particle tracer pointer has been added BUT NOT YET TESTED!

	18 JAN 2024:
	Added check about nvar_min == nmetals
	May not be appropriate if other passive variables are included, e.g. a colour tracer.

	25 JAN 2024:
	Added a counter for particle that are tossed because they are moved beyond the box in the previous time step.
	Added capability to load *additional* DICE ICs
	Removed unnecessary MPI_BCAST clauses

	28 FEB 2024:
	Added family tag, previously set to 0 by default, now set to the value specified by the ICs (if available)

	06 MAR 2024:
	Introduced two new DICE input parameters, ic_scale_metalO/Fe, to weigh the O/Fe initial abundance ratios (previously hard-coded to a value of 0.333)

	18 MAR 2024
	Added two DICE input parameters, ic_scale_metalO/Fe, missing from read_params.f90 (on 06 MAR 2024 added to init_part.f90 by mistake only)

TO DO:

	- Remove obsolete bits such as uu for particles, etc.

Notes:

	- When loading additional DICE ICs, there may be a potential issue with duplicate particle ids (iord)
		- ASSES AND FIX

	- Gas particle (cell) number and gas mass increases slightly at restart, presumably due to the fact that IG_rho != 0
		- ASSES AND FIX

	- Particles at or beyond the box boundary will be tossed at restart

About:

A merge of my dice_restart patch and the oagertz/dice patch.

USAGE:

In the NML, use:

&RESTART_PARAMS
nrestart2=N			! restart at snapshot N
add_dice_ic=.true.  ! optional; to load additional DICE ICS at restart
restart_vars=6,7   	!-> corresponds to the actual indices of passive scalars (excluding temperature)
/

&INIT_PARAMS
filetype='ramses_dice'
/

&RUN_PARAMS
nrestart=0
/
